      "bookTitle": "The Systems View of Life",
      "author": "Fritjof Capra & Pier Luigi Luisi",
      "category": "Psychology",
      "type": "concept",
      "headline": "Epigenetics: The Porous Genome",
      "body": "The dogma that DNA serves as an unalterable master blueprint dictating biology has been superseded.\nThe genome functions like an interactive library: contextual signals, stress hormones, nutrition, and environmental feedback determine which genetic chapters are activated or silenced.",
      "quote": "The genome is not an isolated command center, but part of a complex, interactive cellular network.",
      "actionItem": "Shape an environment that brings out your best instincts: curate your workspace, relationships, and informational diet.",
