      "author": "Fritjof Capra & Pier Luigi Luisi",
      "category": "Psychology",
      "type": "concept",
      "headline": "Bifurcation Points: The Leap into New Order",
      "body": "When a living system moves far from equilibrium, internal tensions reach a critical threshold known as a bifurcation point.\nAt this tipping point, the system cannot maintain its old form; it either collapses into disorder or makes a spontaneous leap into a higher, more sophisticated level of organization.",
      "quote": "At the bifurcation point, the system can branch off into entirely new states of order.",
      "actionItem": "When a project hits a point of acute breakdown, resist the urge to patch up old workflows.\nLook for the higher-order restructuring it invites.",
