      "bookId": "the-systems-view-of-life",
      "bookTitle": "The Systems View of Life",
      "author": "Fritjof Capra & Pier Luigi Luisi",
      "category": "Psychology",
      "type": "actionable",
      "headline": "Cultivate Qualitative Thinking",
      "body": "Modern economics and corporate dashboards fixate obsessively on quantitative metrics: revenue growth, body mass index, gross domestic product.\nBiological health is inherently qualitative: vitality, relational trust, aesthetic joy, resilience.\nWhen quality is sacrificed for pure quantity, pathology ensues.",
      "quote": "Nature does not maximize single variables; it optimizes the balance among many interconnected dimensions.",
      "actionItem": "Introduce at least one qualitative indicator (such as team psychological safety or customer delight) into your primary success scorecard.",
